1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,737
You do not need total readiness to start.

2
00:00:02,737 --> 00:00:04,448
You need minimum viable readiness.

3
00:00:04,448 --> 00:00:07,528
This lesson is about are you ready to start.

4
00:00:07,528 --> 00:00:09,239
Minimum viable readiness vs perfectionism.

5
00:00:09,239 --> 00:00:11,634
Do not treat this as theory only.

6
00:00:11,634 --> 00:00:15,056
Treat it as a move you can run this week.

7
00:00:15,056 --> 00:00:20,188
By the end, you should be able to act without waiting for a perfect plan.

8
00:00:20,188 --> 00:00:23,952
Keep the DigProg habit: watch, practice, then take one real action.

9
00:00:24,272 --> 00:00:32,975
You need four things: a problem you understand, a way to reach about twenty people, an offer draft, and five to ten honest hours each week.

10
00:00:32,975 --> 00:00:35,318
Remember the objective: list readiness gaps honestly.

11
00:00:35,318 --> 00:00:38,999
Write the idea in your own words before you move on.

12
00:00:38,999 --> 00:00:43,016
Name one concrete next action you can finish in under an hour.

13
00:00:43,336 --> 00:00:46,394
You do not need an LLC on day one.

14
00:00:46,394 --> 00:00:50,812
You do not need a logo, a perfect site, or an ads budget.

15
